      "task": "find rose_bush",
      "milestone_id": "find_rose_bush",
      "description": "Uses position_near_with_facing because this is a find/locate/observe task. The player must navigate close enough to the rose bush (within 16 blocks) and face toward it (within 60° tolerance). The rose bush is at spawn-relative (7, 0, 6), so the target is set to [7, 1, 6] (using y=1 to target the center of the two-block-tall flower for better facing calculation). max_distance=5 ensures the player has actually navigated to the rose bush area rather than just being at spawn, while facing_tolerance=60 confirms the player is looking at it. This rule type is preferred over position_inside_box for find tasks because it models 'player can see the target' by combining proximity and facing direction.",
